 "standard_text": "5.4H represent and solve problems related to perimeter and/or area and related to volume",
 "meta_desc": "Free Grade 5 worksheets for Texas TEKS 5.4H: perimeter and area of rectangles, missing sides, volume with V = l × w × h and V = B × h, choosing the right measure and multi-step word problems. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Perimeter goes around, area covers, volume fills.",
 "key_sub": "P = 2l + 2w, A = l × w, V = l × w × h = B × h.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li><b>Perimeter</b> is the distance around: P = 2 × l + 2 × w. It is measured in units (feet).</li><li><b>Area</b> is the space inside a flat shape: A = l × w. It is measured in square units.</li><li><b>Volume</b> is the space inside a solid: V = l × w × h, or V = B × h where B is the area of the base. It is measured in cubic units.</li><li>To find a missing side, work backward with the formula.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>A garden is 20 ft by 12 ft. Fencing costs $4 per foot.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>P = 2 × 20 + 2 × 12 = 64 ft</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>64 × $4</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: $256</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>A box is 8 in by 5 in by 6 in. Find V.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>V = 8 × 5 × 6</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 240 cubic inches</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Adding only two sides for perimeter</td><td>A rectangle has four sides: add l + w, then double it.</td></tr><tr><td>Mixing up area and perimeter</td><td>Inside a shape is area (square units); around it is perimeter.</td></tr><tr><td>Adding the edges of a prism</td><td>Volume multiplies: l × w × h.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does TEKS 5.4H ask?",
   "a": "Represent and solve problems related to perimeter and/or area and related to volume."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is the difference between area and volume?",
   "a": "Area measures a flat surface in square units. Volume measures the space inside a solid in cubic units."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is B in V = B × h?",
   "a": "B is the area of the base. For a rectangular prism, B = l × w."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I find a missing length from the area?",
   "a": "Divide the area by the known side."
  }
 ],
